18
00:00:55,480 --> 00:01:00,080
The story behind Euler Finance is one of the most gripping in crypto's recent history,

19
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:02,640
and it's the one that we're going to explore and tell today.

20
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:08,320
Michael Bentley founded Euler in December of 2020 alongside Doug Hoyt and Jack Pryor

21
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:12,240
with the intent to build a decentralized crypto lending and borrowing platform out of his

22
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:14,560
hometown of Leeds in the UK.

23
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:19,240
Unlike many founders who entered crypto at the time from finance or software, Bentley

24
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:23,680
actually came with seven years of postgraduate research in computational and mathematical

25
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:25,120
biology.

26
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:29,440
That background became foundational to Euler's design, which we'll discuss further.

27
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:33,840
Bentley drew inspiration from control theory, a branch of engineering and applied mathematics

28
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:40,280
focused on influencing dynamic systems, like biological processes or machines, to build

29
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,040
Euler's interest rate model.

30
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:46,320
Where other crypto lending platforms at the time relied on manually set rates, Bentley

31
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:50,760
and the Euler team implemented feedback loops that allowed interest rates to adjust automatically

32
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:53,180
in response to market conditions.

33
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:57,860
As you later put it, what got me excited was the potential to apply my background in

34
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:03,780
system dynamics and control theory to a new kind of open, programmable financial system,

35
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:07,060
that being crypto and smart contract enabled finance.

36
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:12,460
Euler raised multiple rounds of venture capital and launched on Ethereum in late 2021.

37
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:18,940
Despite immediate macro headwinds, Bitcoin plummeting from nearly $70,000 to below $20,000,

38
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:23,180
Euler gained traction, attracting over $500 million of deposits and establishing itself

39
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:25,700
as a key player in DeFi.

40
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:31,540
Then on March 13th of 2023, disaster struck abruptly.

41
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:36,660
In just 15 minutes, Euler was exploited for nearly $200 million, one of the largest hacks

42
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:38,660
in DeFi history.

43
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:42,780
The Euler team launched a three-week hunt to identify the attacker while managing an

44
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:45,580
understandably shaken community.

45
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:48,000
Against the odds, they succeeded.

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,400
Not just in tracing the individual, but in opening lines of direct communication.

47
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:57,840
Bentley ended up developing a personal relationship with the attacker, and through weeks of negotiation

48
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:02,320
and coordination, Euler pulled off a stunning full recovery of the stolen funds.

49
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:06,240
At that point, most assumed Euler would fully wind down.

50
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:10,000
Return remaining capital, shutter operations, and walk away.

51
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,860
But one thing became apparent.

52
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:15,720
The team widely had ambitions to continue building in this space, even if it would not

53
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,600
be with Euler.

54
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:21,800
Investors among the core contributors revealed this shared ambition to keep building.

55
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:27,040
So they asked themselves, if they were to keep going, why not keep going with Euler?

56
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:32,040
Ultimately, backed by the full support of their investors, the team regrouped and rebuilt.

57
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:37,060
Eleven months ago, I spoke to Michael just before the relaunch of Euler v2.

58
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:41,720
At the time, the protocol had only a few stray dollars in deposits and faced considerable

59
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,120
skepticism.

60
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:50,260
Fast forward to today, Euler has grown to over $2.5 billion in deposits, nearly 5x its

61
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:55,680
peak before the hack, and has earned a reputation as a leading lending and borrowing platform

62
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:58,760
across multiple chains and asset types.

63
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:02,680
It's a story of conviction, resilience, and redemption.

64
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:07,640
Today, I had the privilege of sitting down again with Michael to talk through that journey

65
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,040
and the road ahead.

66
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:12,800
For disclosure, Castle Island Ventures is an investor in Euler and remains a strong

67
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:15,680
supporter of the team moving forward.

68
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:19,760
Without further ado, here's my conversation with Michael Bentley.

69
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:25,400
Michael, first off, I want to open by saying I can't speak to the amount of respect that

70
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:31,720
I and the team have for you and the Euler team's resilience and commitment to everything

71
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:35,840
you've done in the wake of the experience that you've had over four years.

72
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:38,780
And we speak about it often as something that we deeply admire.

73
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:43,260
And it's incredible to have you back after we spoke about a year, a year and a half ago

74
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,580
before V2 launched.

75
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:47,160
And it's incredible what's happened in that time span.

76
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:50,940
So I wanted to say that first, and I find an incredibly moving story because in the

77
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:56,120
backdrop of crypto, which so often functions with anonymity being a norm, you can't tell

78
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,120
who wallets are.

79
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,500
